title = "parking-domain — a 3-floor, 50-spot lot view with live occupancy and history"

text = """
Extend the EXISTING `components/parking-domain` (already shipped — read
`src/handlers.rs` and `src/lib.rs` in full before changing anything) with
three new routes. Nothing about the existing routes changes: `POST
/api/spots`, `GET /api/spots`, `POST /api/spots/{id}/reservations`, `GET
/api/reservations`, `POST /api/reservations/{id}/cancel` all keep behaving
exactly as they do today — the held-out scenario in `context` below
re-asserts every one of them BEFORE the new routes are ever touched, so a
regression there fails just as hard as a wrong new route.

## The three new routes

  POST   /api/lot/seed                {}                    (admin)
  GET    /api/lot                                            (any authenticated)
  GET    /api/spots/{id}/history                             (admin)

### `POST /api/lot/seed`

Idempotent. Ensures exactly 150 spots exist in the SAME `spots` collection
every other route already uses — 3 floors (1, 2, 3), 50 spots each
(numbered 1-50) — by ADDING two new fields to the spot document, `floor:
u32` and `number: u32` (a spot created through the existing `POST
/api/spots` has neither field; a lot-seeded spot has both). Label each
seeded spot e.g. `"F1-01"` .. `"F3-50"` (floor and zero-padded number).

Idempotent means: call it once, it creates 150 spots. Call it again, it
creates NOTHING more — same shape as `guest_owner_or_admin_policy!`'s own
idempotent rule registration in `components/guestauth/src/lib.rs` (in
`context` below): a marker record in a `meta` collection
(`{"kind":"lot_seeded"}`, indexed on `kind`) that a second call checks for
before creating anything. Response, both times, `200` with
`{"total": 150}` — the actual current count of lot-seeded spots (floor and
number both present), not a count of every ad-hoc spot in the collection.

### `GET /api/lot`

Any authenticated caller. Returns every lot-seeded spot (floor and number
both present — NOT the ad-hoc spots `POST /api/spots` creates, which have
neither field), grouped by floor:

    {"floors": [
      {"floor": 1, "spots": [{"id":"...", "number":1, "taken":false}, … 50 total, ordered by number …]},
      {"floor": 2, "spots": [ … 50 … ]},
      {"floor": 3, "spots": [ … 50 … ]}
    ]}

`taken` is computed FRESH on every call, never stored: a spot is taken if
ANY reservation on it has `status == "active"` AND its window covers the
current moment — `start <= now < end`, the exact same half-open comparison
`create_report`'s (a nearby sibling goal, and this file's own overlap
check) uses. `now` is `crate::now_secs()`, already available here via
`guestauth::guest_audit!` in `lib.rs` — no new import needed. If the lot has
never been seeded, `floors` is an empty list (never 404, never an error —
seeding is a setup step, and reading the lot before it exists is not a
crime).

### `GET /api/spots/{id}/history`

Admin only. Every reservation ever made on that spot — active AND
cancelled, oldest first — regardless of whether the spot is a lot-seeded
one or an ad-hoc one:

    {"spot_id": "...", "reservations": [
      {"id":"...", "subject":"...", "start":<u64>, "end":<u64>, "status":"active"|"cancelled"},
      …
    ]}

A spot with no reservations yet returns `"reservations": []`, `200` — not
a 404 (a 404 is for a spot that does not exist at all; check
`records::get("spots", id)` first and 404 only if that fails).

## Reuse what already exists in this file

`introspect`, `is_admin`, `records::create`/`get`/`update`/`list_records`/
`find_by`, `Reply::json`/`Reply::err`, and `entries_json` all already exist
in this file — use them exactly as the existing routes do, do not
reinvent any of them. `now_secs()` is a top-level function in this crate
(from `guestauth::guest_audit!` in `lib.rs`), reachable as `crate::now_secs()`.

## The static SPA

`examples/parking/public/index.html` — add a "Lot" view: a button any
logged-in user can click to see the lot (a grid or table per floor, 50
cells, colored/marked to distinguish taken from free at a glance), and
(admin only) a "seed the lot" button and, when a lot spot is selected, a
history list for it. Read the file's current content first (it already has
login/register, spot list, reservation form, my-reservations — match its
existing style and `fetch` conventions, do not rewrite what already works).
"""

base_paths = [
  "components/parking-domain/",
  "components/auth-guard/",
  "components/policy-guard/",
  "components/record-store/",
  "components/audit-log/",
  "components/rate-limiter/",
  "components/guestauth/",
  "components/guestio/",
  "components/guestfmt/",
  "components/Cargo.toml",
  "wit/",
  "host/wit/deps/",
]

writable = [
  "components/parking-domain/src/handlers.rs",
  "examples/parking/public/index.html",
]

workspace_manifest = "components/Cargo.toml"
keep_members = [
  "parking-domain",
  "auth-guard",
  "policy-guard",
  "record-store",
  "audit-log",
  "rate-limiter",
  "guestauth",
  "guestio",
  "guestfmt",
]

context = [
  "components/parking-domain/src/lib.rs",
  "components/parking-domain/Cargo.toml",
  "components/parking-domain/wit/parking-domain.wit",
  "components/guestauth/src/lib.rs",
  "components/record-store/wit/record.wit",
  ".comp/context/auth-consumer.wit",
  # The held-out judge: every existing assertion re-checked, then the new
  # lot/history flow appended after it. Not writable — shown so a branch
  # knows the exact route contracts instead of guessing wrong.
  "components/parking-domain/gate.sh",
  "components/parking-domain/scenario.hurl",
]

[[check]]
id = "behaves-under-real-http"
required = true
weight = 1
command = ["bash", "components/parking-domain/gate.sh"]
